## 2.2 Analytical framework and PICOs

An initial GDG meeting was held in Geneva in July 2019 to determine the scope and PICO (population, intervention, comparison, outcome) questions of the guideline. The GDG first developed an analytical framework (Fig. 1) that demonstrates the impact of interventions on intermediate and final outcomes and displays the order of the key questions to better visualize and place them along the patient-flow pathway. Following this, and a preliminary scoping review and discussion between the steering group and methodologist, PICO questions were developed. These were considered, deliberated on, further refined and voted on during the meeting.

